WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:06.400
OK, guys, we have to start today with a very
real, very sobering conversation.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.909
I wish we didn't have to have this conversation,
but I'm not going to blow smoke up down in

00:00:12.909 --> 00:00:15.339
out of anywhere.

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:17.080
Maybe we can get something positive out of
it.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:23.140
And I don't say that in a sort of coy or,
you know, kind of B.S. way, a teachable moment.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.480
Like maybe we can actually get something out
of this because it's increasingly clear that

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:34.260
Republicans, if they choose to, if they decide
that the political risks are reasonable, are

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:40.430
going to have the votes to move forward with
a replacement of Ruth Bader Ginsburg on the

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.430
Supreme Court.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.090
Yes, they are hypocrites.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:50.190
Yes, they're completely ignoring the guidelines
they claimed were necessary in 2016 to deny

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:56.350
Barack Obama a Supreme Court pick to replace
the late Justice Antonin Scalia with Merrick

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.610
Garland.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:03.280
But the reality is we have to deal with reality
that Democrats right now don't have a path

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.540
to stopping Donald Trump from replacing Ruth
Bader Ginsburg.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.350
It will be up to Republicans.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:16.180
Remember that the numbers are Republicans
have 53 of the 100 Senate seats.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:22.010
In order to deny them the 51 or it's really
50 votes that they have to be denied because

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.369
even in a 50/50 vote.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:27.320
Mike Pence gets to tie break and you know
how that will go.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:33.049
We need to find four Republicans who will
refuse to move forward with a confirmation.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:35.549
We heard from Lisa Murkowski from Alaska.

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:40.960
She is one such Republican who has said at
least not before the election, during the

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:41.960
lame duck.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:42.960
Who knows?

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.869
We then heard from Susan Collins from Maine,
another Republican senator who says not before

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:49.880
the election.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:55.600
No, but bear in mind, even if we wait it out
until November 3rd.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.759
And Joe Biden wins these, same to Republicans.

00:01:58.759 --> 00:02:03.079
Lisa Murkowski and Susan Collins may well
be willing to push someone through during

00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:04.590
a lame duck period.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:08.239
And in any case, too, isn't going to be enough
to stop it.

00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:13.130
Donald, Mitt Romney, rather, is someone that
people have been looking towards.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.290
Maybe Mitt Romney could be a third Republican.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:20.780
As of right now, Mitt Romney has said it looks
like he's going to be okay moving forward.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.790
And even if Mitt Romney could be added as
number three to the list, you need a fourth.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:27.599
So the reality today.

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:32.120
Is we have to contend with this situation.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:38.730
There is a very real practical lesson here
and it's a lesson to all of those people.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:39.730
You remember them?

